@article{Werner2012,
annote = {MV = PQ excludes financial transactions. Original conception was PT for all transactions. 



How is money created and injected in our present-day system? This is a simple 
question that empirical research should quickly be able to answer. Intriguingly, 
virtually no research is published on this question at all in the leading journals of 
macroeconomics, monetary economics, or banking and finance.

Since the credit market is rationed and determines the money supply, the quantity and  the quality of credit creation are key factors shaping the economy. This explains why 
