@article{Reitwiessner2016,
abstract = {The possibilities of zkSNARKs are impressive, you can verify the correctness of computations without having to execute them and you will not even learn what was executed – just that it was done correctly. Unfortunately, most explanations of zkSNARKs resort to hand-waving at some point and thus they remain something " magical " , suggesting that only the most enlightened actually understand how and why (and if?) they work. The reality is that zkSNARKs can be reduced to four simple techniques and this blog post aims to explain them. Anyone who can understand how the RSA cryptosystem works, should also get a pretty good understanding of currently employed zkSNARKs. Let's see if it will achieve its goal! As a very short summary, zkSNARKs as currently implemented, have 4 main ingredients (don't worry, we will explain all the terms in later sections):},
