abstract = {We study functions g$\alpha$(x) which are one-sided, heavy-tailed L{\'{e}}vy stable probability distributions of index $\alpha$, 0<$\alpha$<1, of fundamental importance in random systems, for anomalous diffusion and fractional kinetics. We furnish exact and explicit expressions for g$\alpha$(x), 0≤x<∞ for all $\alpha$=l/k<1, with k and l positive integers. We reproduce all the known results given by k≤4 and present many new exact solutions for k>4, all expressed in terms of known functions. This will allow a "fine-tuning" of $\alpha$ in order to adapt g$\alpha$(x) to a given experimental situation. {\textcopyright} 2010 The American Physical Society.},
